.claude/
target/
.DS_Store

# Local crash-recovery snapshots written by scene_editor_web's atomic save
# (scene_io.write_json_atomic). Recovery state, not content -- committing them
# would grow the repo by a copy of every scene on every save.
.history/

# The material library is installed on demand, not committed.
#
# Same reasoning as the terrain starter set, taken one step further. A small
# committed set exists so the engine renders properly out of the box
# (textures/terrain/), but the LIBRARY is unbounded -- it is where a level's
# whole palette accumulates, one 250KB material at a time, and git keeps every
# version of a binary forever. Replacing one material would double its cost in
# history for a file nobody diffs.
#
# A fresh clone therefore starts with an empty library and untextured grey
# brushes, which is an honest blockout state; "+ Add materials" is in the
# picker, and an install takes a second or two.
materials/
